From 0a9712a0144df8feccdd7ab690829288dbd76b95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gavin John <gavinnjohn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 04:08:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 69/69] demux: asf: stop the pcr where the data stops

The demux loop walks its clock forward in fixed steps and sends each
step as a pcr, having first handed over everything that falls inside it.
At the end of the stream it takes one more step than it has data for:
the last round dequeues nothing and still advances, so the last pcr
describes a tenth of a second of silence that is not in the file.

Nothing used to notice, because the stream was over. A repeat does: it
resumes the next pass from as far as this one reached, and that is now a
step further out than the file goes, leaving a hole of whatever the file
does not divide - 61 ms here, up to a full step.

Only step while there is data to cover, or while the stream is still
running.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 modules/demux/asf/asf.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/asf/asf.c b/modules/demux/asf/asf.c
index 31d98855ea..a77df8112b 100644
--- a/modules/demux/asf/asf.c
+++ b/modules/demux/asf/asf.c
@@ -257,7 +257,11 @@ static int Demux( demux_t *p_demux )
     {
         bool b_data = Block_Dequeue( p_demux, p_sys->i_time + CHUNK );
 
-        if( p_sys->i_time != VLC_TICK_INVALID )
+        /* Once the data has run out there is nothing left for another step to
+         * cover, and a pcr past the end of the data describes silence that was
+         * never in the file. A repeat resumes the next pass from where this
+         * one reached, so an overshoot here is a hole there. */
+        if( p_sys->i_time != VLC_TICK_INVALID && ( b_data || !p_sys->b_eos ) )
         {
             p_sys->i_time += CHUNK;
             p_sys->b_pcr_sent = true;
